## What this oracle is

A QiForge oracle on **Cloudflare Workers**, built on `@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers`. The runtime brings the HTTP/SSE shell (UCAN auth on every request), one Durable Object per user (their SQLite working copy and the agent turn), the Matrix gateway object, the agent graph and the bundled plugins. **You** ship the oracle's identity, prompt slots and plugins.

- **Organization:** {{org}}
- **Runtime:** `@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers` — ships as TypeScript source; read it in `node_modules/@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers/src`
- **Reference oracle:** https://github.com/ixoworld/qiforge/tree/main/apps/qiforge-workers-example
- **Public docs:** https://docs.ixo.world/build-an-oracle

## Layout

```
src/
├── index.ts        # createOracleWorker({ config, plugins }) + export { UserOracleDO, MatrixGatewayDO }
├── gateway.ts      # createGatewayWorker() — the Matrix gateway script
├── config.ts       # identity + prompt slots
└── plugins/        # custom plugins — one folder per plugin
wrangler.jsonc          # oracle script (vars, Durable Objects, rate limit, aliases, minify)
wrangler.gateway.jsonc  # gateway script
.dev.vars               # local secrets (gitignored)
```

Each custom plugin lives at `src/plugins/<name>/<name>.plugin.ts` with a colocated `<name>.plugin.test.ts`. Nothing is auto-discovered: every plugin is passed in `plugins: []` in `src/index.ts`.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` | `wrangler dev` with both scripts (http://localhost:8787) |
| `pnpm test` | Unit tests inside workerd |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Type-check |
| `pnpm run build` | `wrangler deploy --dry-run` for both scripts |
| `pnpm run deploy` | Deploy the gateway script, then the oracle script |
| `qiforge-cli plugin new <name>` | Scaffold a plugin into `src/plugins/<name>/` |

